<title>USA: Haggar unit to close Weslaco plant.</title>
<headline>Haggar unit to close Weslaco plant.</headline>
<dateline>EDINBURG, Texas 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Haggar Clothing Co said on Tuesday it will close a plant in Weslaco, Texas that employs 675 people, and transfer its sewing operations to the company's Edinburg plant.</p>
<p>The company, a subsidiary of Haggar Corp, said the consolidation will cut its manufacturing costs by $12 million to $14 million per year. The charge from the closure was taken during the fourth quarter of fiscal 1996, which ended September 30.</p>
<p>About 175 of the Weslaco employees will be offered transfers to Edinburg. The remaining 500 employees will be offered transfers to other Haggar plants, or given severance packages.</p>
<p>The plant will close on May 2.</p>
